# SABOTAGE: T146 (dogfood W3-E1, SECURITY-HIGH) gate sabotage — defeats the operator control-plane
# ROLE authorization in ALL THREE places T146 wired it:
#   (1) `Samen.Web.Operator.Authz.validate_role/1` fail-closed catch-all: nil -> :operator_admin
#       (the by-construction on_mount now admits any principal on the WEBSOCKET/HTTP LiveView mount);
#   (2) `Samen.Web.AuthGate.operator_role/2` fail-closed catch-all: nil -> :operator_admin
#       (the conn-level pipeline now admits any authenticated principal);
#   (3) driftwood's `/operator/impersonate` live_session: REMOVES the `require_operator` on_mount
#       (the round-3 live-nav gate), so the router no longer carries the hook there.
# With (1)+(2) a plain authenticated TENANT user again reaches every /operator/* surface — the
# accounts/billing console (cross-tenant admin email + org + MRR in the clear) AND the surfaces
# mounted OUTSIDE samen_operator_routes/2 (the portfolio AGGREGATE's operator-confidential
# MRR/volume, the impersonation console, the operator desk-chat). (3) additionally strips the
# impersonate live-nav authz so the introspection guard for the round-3 fix flips. The POSITIVE
# CONTROLs (a genuine rostered operator) stay green (they validated to a real role either way),
# so the flip is non-vacuous. Keeping each clause (vs deleting the guard) avoids orphaning
# helpers. Reverts byte-exact (all three files).
# APP: driftwood
# TEST_FILES: test/operator_authz_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: RED: tenant-user GET /operator/accounts is redirected to /login
# MUST_FAIL: RED: tenant-user GET /operator/aggregate is refused
# MUST_FAIL: /operator/impersonate is in its OWN named operator live_session
